{
  "an8.76:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 8.76 ",
  "an8.76:0.2": "8. Pairs ",
  "an8.76:0.3": "Accomplishments (2nd) ",
  "an8.76:1.1": "“Mendicants, there are these eight accomplishments. ",
  "an8.76:1.2": "What eight? ",
  "an8.76:1.3": "Accomplishment in initiative, protection, good friendship, and balanced finances. And accomplishment in faith, ethics, generosity, and wisdom. ",
  "an8.76:1.4": "And what is accomplishment in initiative? ",
  "an8.76:1.5": "It’s when a gentleman earns a living by means such as ",
  "an8.76:1.6": "farming, trade, raising cattle, archery, government service, or one of the professions. ",
  "an8.76:1.7": "He understands how to go about these things in order to complete and organize the work. ",
  "an8.76:1.8": "This is called accomplishment in initiative. ",
  "an8.76:2.1": "And what is accomplishment in protection? ",
  "an8.76:2.2": "It’s when a gentleman owns legitimate wealth that he has earned by his own efforts and initiative, built up with his own hands, gathered by the sweat of the brow. He ensures it is guarded and protected, thinking: ",
  "an8.76:2.3": "‘How can I prevent my wealth from being taken by rulers or bandits, consumed by fire, swept away by flood, or taken by unloved heirs?’ ",
  "an8.76:2.4": "This is called accomplishment in protection. ",
  "an8.76:3.1": "And what is accomplishment in good friendship? ",
  "an8.76:3.2": "It’s when a gentleman resides in a town or village. And in that place there are householders or their children who may be y